&lt;p&gt;Regular calendars are great at showing &lt;em&gt;when&lt;/em&gt; things happen, but they never stop you from overbooking yourself. They don't care if two sprints collide or if your rest buffer drops to zero.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So I built &lt;strong&gt;Dev Cadence&lt;/strong&gt; — a &lt;strong&gt;free, open-source Chrome Side Panel extension&lt;/strong&gt; I use every day to plan my own sprints, hackathons, and rest days.&lt;/p&gt;

