&lt;h2&gt;


  Agent Q
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pressing the &lt;code&gt;Q&lt;/code&gt; key takes you into model editor mode. If your cursor is hovering over an object, it will select that object. If you're pointing at empty space, you'll get a cube with the material currently selected in the &lt;code&gt;P&lt;/code&gt; palette.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can then edit it using the familiar Blender keyboard shortcuts. Hopefully, I've included them all in the Help section.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'll write about this in more detail later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can try the evolving development environment online at &lt;a href="https://spider-paint.vercel.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://spider-paint.vercel.app/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Five Percent, my competition entry, is essentially a snapshot of this development environment.&lt;/p&gt;

